expression/parser.ts adapts expression grammar, operators, state and builtin
function semantics from pinned FFmpeg libavutil/eval.c (Copyright (c) 2002-2006
Michael Niedermayer; Copyright (c) 2006 Oded Shimon). expression/sfc64.ts adapts
libavutil/sfc64.h (Copyright (c) 2024 Michael Niedermayer).

expression/glibc-hypot.ts adapts the non-FMA path of glibc 2.36
sysdeps/ieee754/dbl-64/e_hypot.c, Copyright (C) 2021-2022 Free Software
Foundation, Inc. glibc-log.ts, glibc-exp2.ts and glibc-tables.ts adapt e_log.c,
e_exp2.c, e_log_data.c and e_exp_data.c from the same glibc version,
Copyright (C) 2018-2022 Free Software Foundation, Inc. These adaptations
retain LGPL-2.1-or-later. Reference source URLs and hashes are documented in
docs/contributing/expressions.md.

Numeric profiles are scoped to the recorded reference environments. C errno,
floating exception flags, full diagnostic routing, complete resource accounting
and exhaustive libm conformance remain incomplete. This scheduling/expression
work does not complete the project-wide license audit.

thread-frame-queue.ts adapts the FIFO, finish-bit and choke transitions from
FFmpeg fftools/thread_queue.c at commit
946fcce07b6dcd0331c8cc609192aeff5e1924f8, licensed LGPL-2.1-or-later.
The TypeScript wait/cancellation/budget and accepted-lease snapshot mechanisms
adapt those transitions for cooperative single-isolate execution. No native
threads or FFmpeg runtime dependency are introduced. Native oracle source is
in tools/differential-runner/thread-frame-queue/oracle.c; that developer-only
program includes the pinned upstream source under the same license.

bounded-rational.ts adapts av_reduce from FFmpeg libavutil/rational.c at commit
946fcce07b6dcd0331c8cc609192aeff5e1924f8, Copyright (c) 2003 Michael Niedermayer,
licensed LGPL-2.1-or-later. Native differential evidence is generated by the
developer-only tools/differential-runner/bounded-rational/oracle.c linked against
the pinned reference library. No FFmpeg runtime dependency is introduced.

number-rational.ts adapts av_d2q from the same pinned FFmpeg libavutil/rational.c,
Copyright (c) 2003 Michael Niedermayer, LGPL-2.1-or-later. The developer-only
number-rational oracle calls av_d2q with raw IEEE bits; runtime uses TypeScript
and the public bounded rational kernel, with no FFmpeg runtime dependency.

channel-layout.ts adapts the default-layout table selection of fixed FFmpeg
libavutil/channel_layout.c at commit946fcce07b6dcd0331c8cc609192aeff5e1924f8.
Copyright (c)2006 Michael Niedermayer <michaelni@gmx.at>.
LGPL-2.1-or-later;see LICENSES/LGPL-2.1-or-later.txt and pinned upstream source.
The TypeScript table preserves wide native masks as bigint;it does not implement
arbitrary layouts or all channel-layout operations.
